      "content": "i know, i know. i've heard the \"you are worthy\" speech before. but it feels so hollow when the actual substance of my life is just... erased. my career, my community, my entire identity was tied to that presence. now that it's stripped away, there's nothing left but this empty shell. it's like the person who mattered is dead, so what's the point of even keeping the body around? it's just a placeholder for someone who isn't there anymore.",
